screen.EVENTS_SCREEN=Events
screen.FLOWER_FESTIVAL_SCREEN=Flower Festival
option.FLOWER_FESTIVAL=Flower Festival
option.FLOWER_FESTIVAL.comment=Flowers start to glow with the color of their petals. The closer a flower is to the player, the brighter; distant ones fade out. With LPV enabled, flowers also light up the ground around them in their own color.
option.EVENT_FLOWER_BRIGHTNESS=Glow brightness
option.EVENT_FLOWER_BRIGHTNESS.comment=How strongly flowers glow during the event.
option.EVENT_FLOWER_FADE_START=Fade start
option.EVENT_FLOWER_FADE_START.comment=Distance to the player where flowers glow at full strength. Fading begins beyond it.
option.EVENT_FLOWER_FADE_END=Fade end
option.EVENT_FLOWER_FADE_END.comment=Distance to the player at which the glow disappears completely.

screen.DH_SCREEN=Distant Horizons
option.DH_SEAM_MARGIN=LoD seam margin §e[?]
option.DH_SEAM_MARGIN.comment=How many blocks before vanilla render distance DH terrain is fully faded in. Lower = LoD starts closer and hides the vanilla/DH seam
option.DH_SEAM_WIDTH=LoD seam width
option.DH_SEAM_DITHER=Dithered LoD seam §e[?]
option.DH_SEAM_DITHER.comment=Softens the vanilla/DH transition. Disable only if you see noisy dots at the seam
option.DH_TERRAIN_NOISE=LOD terrain noise
option.DH_SHADOW_ENABLED=LOD shadow casters §e[?]
option.DH_SHADOW_ENABLED.comment=Lets Distant Horizons write into the shadow map. Does not shade LoD past shadow distance — use contact shadows for that
option.DH_FOLIAGE_SSS=LOD foliage SSS §e[?]
option.DH_FOLIAGE_SSS.comment=Wrap lighting on LoD leaves so tree cubes are not full-bright
option.DH_AO=LOD ambient occlusion §e[?]
option.DH_AO.comment=Screen-space AO on Distant Horizons terrain (crevices between hills and tree clusters)
option.DH_DEPTH_SHADOWS=LOD contact shadows §e[?]
option.DH_DEPTH_SHADOWS.comment=Traces the sun against vanilla + LoD depth so distant trees receive contact shadows without a huge shadow map
option.DH_DEPTH_SHADOW_STEPS=Contact shadow steps

screen.LPV_SCREEN=Colored blocklight
option.LPV_ENABLED=Colored blocklight (LPV) §e[?]
option.LPV_ENABLED.comment=True voxel flood fill. Terrain around you is written into a light volume from the shadow pass and flooded outwards every frame, so torches, glowstone and lava each cast their own color and it bends around corners. Replaces the vanilla blocklight ramp entirely. Iris only, and it adds a shadow pass in the Nether and the End
option.LPV_SIZE=Volume size §e[?]
option.LPV_SIZE.comment=Side of the voxel cube in blocks, centered on you. Light outside it is gone, so this is also the range. Costs memory and compute as the cube of itself
option.LPV_BRIGHTNESS=Brightness
option.LPV_BRIGHTNESS.comment=1.0 matches the vanilla torch ramp. Higher values only add extra energy on top of that.
option.LPV_FALLOFF=Falloff §e[?]
option.LPV_FALLOFF.comment=How much light survives one voxel of travel, so it sets how far a source reaches. High values carry light deep into caves but also wash out the shape of a room
option.LPV_DAY_LEAK=Daylight leak §e[?]
option.LPV_DAY_LEAK.comment=What is left of colored blocklight in full sun. Torches read at full strength in a dark cave either way; this only decides how much they still tint a surface at noon
option.LPV_SATURATION=Source saturation
option.LPV_SATURATION.comment=Saturation of the light source palette. 0 makes every source white.
option.LPV_TINT_SATURATION=Glass saturation
option.LPV_TINT_SATURATION.comment=Saturation of the stained glass tints light picks up passing through them.
option.AIR_FOG=3D air fog §e[?]
option.AIR_FOG.comment=Volumetric haze: blue distance (Rayleigh) + ground/sunset glow (Mie). Height-based, so peaks poke through. Replaces overworld distance fog. Marches to Distant Horizons range when DH is loaded
option.AIR_FOG_STRENGTH=3D fog strength
option.AIR_FOG_DENSITY=Rayleigh density §e[?]
option.AIR_FOG_DENSITY.comment=Blue atmospheric haze with distance. Stronger = farther terrain dissolves into sky
option.AIR_FOG_MIE=Mie haze §e[?]
option.AIR_FOG_MIE.comment=Low white/golden fog near the ground. Stronger at dawn, dusk and in rain
option.AIR_FOG_HEIGHT=Altitude falloff §e[?]
option.AIR_FOG_HEIGHT.comment=How high the fog stays dense. Lower = fog hugs valleys; higher = haze fills more of the sky
option.AIR_FOG_SAMPLES=3D fog samples
option.AIR_FOG_SAMPLES.comment=More steps = smoother height layers on DH terrain. 12 is usually enough
option.AIR_FOG_RAIN=Rain fog boost
option.AIR_FOG_NOISE=Cloudy fog §e[?]
option.AIR_FOG_NOISE.comment=Soft noise blobs in the Mie layer. Most visible at dawn in valleys

option.AIR_FOG_RAIN.comment=Rain boost for volumetric air fog.
option.AIR_FOG_STRENGTH.comment=How strongly 3D fog “eats” the distance and atmospheric depth.
option.AO_MODE.comment=AO calculation mode (SSAO / GTAO).
option.AO_RADIUS.comment=Sampling radius for AO.
option.AO_SAMPLES.comment=Number of AO samples. Higher = smoother, but heavier.
option.AO_STRENGTH.comment=AO darkening intensity.
option.AUTO_EXPOSURE_STRENGTH.comment=Auto exposure strength: how actively brightness changes.
option.CLOUD_LC_DENSITY.comment=Density of the low (LC) cloud layer.
option.CLOUD_LC_DETAIL.comment=Detail level of the low cloud layer.
option.CLOUD_LC_DISTANCE.comment=Draw distance of low clouds.
option.CLOUD_MC_DENSITY.comment=Density of the mid (MC) cloud layer.
option.CLOUD_MC_DETAIL.comment=Detail level of the mid cloud layer.
option.CLOUD_MC_DISTANCE.comment=Draw distance of mid clouds.
option.CLOUD_UC_DENSITY.comment=Density of the high (UC) cloud layer.
option.CLOUD_UC_DETAIL.comment=Detail level of the high cloud layer.
option.CLOUD_UC_DISTANCE.comment=Draw distance of high clouds.
option.DH_DEPTH_SHADOW_STEPS.comment=Contact shadow steps by depth.
option.DH_SEAM_WIDTH.comment=LoD seam smoothing zone width in Distant Horizons (wider = softer transition).
option.DH_TERRAIN_NOISE.comment=LoD terrain noise for a more natural level transition.
option.EMISSION_STRENGTH.comment=Emission strength for materials and blocks with emission.
option.ENABLE_FOG.comment=Enable fog.
option.ENABLE_SHADOWS.comment=Enable shadows.
option.END_STARS_AMOUNT.comment=End starfield density (how many stars are visible).
option.END_STARS_OPACITY.comment=How visible the End stars are over the sky.
option.FOLIAGE_SSS_STRENGTH.comment=Foliage SSS strength against the light.
option.GLOWING_ORES.comment=Enables enhanced glow for glowing ores.
option.HAND_DYNAMIC_LIGHTING.comment=Dynamic lighting coming from the item in your hand.
option.IPBR_REFLECTION_STRENGTH.comment=Reflection strength in IPBR.
option.LIGHT_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Sunlight brightness.
option.MOON_B.comment=Moon blue color component.
option.MOON_G.comment=Moon green color component.
option.MOON_R.comment=Moon red color component.
option.NETHER_FOG_STRENGTH.comment=Fog strength in the Nether.
option.NORMAL_RESOLUTION.comment=Resolution of procedural normals. Higher = more accurate.
option.NORMAL_STRENGTH.comment=Strength of procedural normals.
option.NORMAL_THRESHOLD.comment=Normal generation threshold: separates weak details from noise.
option.OVERWORLD_FOG_MIN_SLIDER.comment=Minimum Overworld fog intensity.
option.REFLECTIONS.comment=Overall reflection opacity (SSR visibility).
option.SHADOW_BLUENESS.comment=Shadow tint: how cold/bluish shadows look.
option.SHADOW_DARKNESS.comment=Overall shadow darkness: how strongly shadows darken areas.
option.SHADOW_ENTITY.comment=Entity shadows.
option.SSR_BINARY_STEPS.comment=Refinement steps at the end of SSR (higher = more accurate, but heavier).
option.SSR_MAX_STEPS.comment=Maximum SSR ray-tracing steps.
option.SSR_STEP_SIZE.comment=SSR step size (smaller = more accurate, larger = faster).
option.STAR_AMOUNT.comment=Starfield density (how many stars are visible).
option.STAR_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Star brightness and overall starfield sparkle.
option.STAR_SIZE.comment=Star size scale.
option.STYLE_CONTRAST.comment=Color grading contrast.
option.STYLE_SATURATION.comment=Color grading saturation.
option.TORCH_INNER_B.comment=Torch color blue component (inner).
option.TORCH_INNER_G.comment=Torch color green component (inner).
option.TORCH_INNER_R.comment=Torch color red component (inner).
option.TORCH_MIDDLE_B.comment=Torch color blue component (middle).
option.TORCH_MIDDLE_G.comment=Torch color green component (middle).
option.TORCH_MIDDLE_R.comment=Torch color red component (middle).
option.TORCH_OUTER_B.comment=Torch color blue component (outer).
option.TORCH_OUTER_G.comment=Torch color green component (outer).
option.TORCH_OUTER_R.comment=Torch color red component (outer).
option.VL_STRENGTH.comment=Volumetric lighting strength (VL).
option.WATER_A.comment=Water opacity: how strongly it hides the ground and volume.
option.WATER_B.comment=Water tint: how cold/bluish it looks.
option.WATER_BRIGHTNESS.comment=How brightly the water surface and nearby reflections glow.
option.WATER_FOG_DENSITY.comment=Underwater fog density by distance (how quickly it darkens with depth).
option.WATER_GLINT_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Glint intensity on water.
option.WATER_GLINT_CUTOFF.comment=Glint visibility threshold: at what angle/brightness glints become stronger.
option.WATER_WAVE_SIZE.comment=Water wave size.
option.WAVING_AMPLITUDE.comment=Waving amplitude of leaves/plants: how much they sway.
option.WAVING_LEAVES.comment=Enable leaf waving.
option.WAVING_PLANTS.comment=Enable plant waving.
option.WEATHER_OPACITY.comment=Weather overlay opacity (how visible the weather effect is).
option.shadowDistance.comment=Shadow distance. Higher = further visible, but heavier.
option.shadowMapResolution.comment=Shadow map resolution. Higher = sharper, but heavier.
